- sublicensing, renting, selling, or commercially exploiting CraftStudio;
- using the CraftStudio name, branding, or artwork for another project; or
- claiming CraftStudio or any derivative version as your own work.

The only authorized public releases are those published by ARCn09 through an
official CraftStudio page or repository.

3. GitHub and contributions

When CraftStudio is hosted in a public GitHub repository, GitHub users may view
and fork the repository only to the extent required by GitHub's Terms of
Service. A GitHub fork does not grant permission to publish releases,
redistribute CraftStudio, operate the fork as a separate project, or distribute
compiled files.

You may submit a patch or pull request directly to the official CraftStudio
repository. By intentionally submitting a contribution, you confirm that you
have the right to submit it and grant ARCn09 a perpetual, worldwide,
irrevocable, royalty-free license to use, reproduce, modify, distribute,
publish, sublicense, and relicense that contribution as part of CraftStudio.

